iy-A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hhavynn/vsa-website/labels/type:chore","name":"type:chore","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11658491899,"node_id":"LA_kwDOO5sMW88AAAACtuZ3-w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hhavynn/vsa-website/labels/area:devex","name":"area:devex","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11658574278,"node_id":"LA_kwDOO5sMW88AAAACtue5xg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hhavynn/vsa-website/labels/agent:codex","name":"agent:codex","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hhavynn/vsa-website/milestones/1","html_url":"https://github.com/hhavynn/vsa-website/milestone/1","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hhavynn/vsa-website/milestones/1/labels","id":17083653,"node_id":"MI_kwDOO5sMW84BBK0F","number":1,"title":"Contributor onboarding","description":"A new contributor can clone, run, and ship a first PR without help. See docs/DEVELOPMENT-ROADMAP.md §10.","creator":{"login":"hhavynn","id":107665875,"node_id":"U_kgDOBmrZ0w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/107665875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hhavynn","html_url":"https://github.com/hhavynn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hhavynn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hhavynn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hhavynn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hhavynn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hhavynn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hhavynn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hhavynn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hhavynn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hhavynn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":8,"closed_issues":4,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-08-01T02:14:04Z","updated_at":"2026-08-01T03:09:13Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-28T20:55:51Z","updated_at":"2026-08-01T02:14:56Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Parent: #314\n\n## Problem\n\n`package-lock.json` is committed (correct), and CI uses `npm ci` (correct). But nothing tells a contributor:\n\n- Use `npm ci`, not `npm install`, for a clean setup — and why the distinction matters\n- What to do when they legitimately need to add a dependency\n- That adding one is a **decision**, not a routine act, on a deprecated CRA toolchain\n- Whether lockfile churn in a PR is expected or a red flag\n\nWith multiple contributors, a stray `npm install` that rewrites the lockfile produces a large, unreviewable diff and can silently change transitive versions.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A short section in `CONTRIBUTING.md` (#295) covering:\n  - `npm ci` for setup and CI; `npm install` only when intentionally changing dependencies\n  - Lockfile changes belong in their own commit, never mixed into a feature diff\n  - Adding a dependency needs justification: is it small, maintained, and worth the bundle cost? (#300 tracks bundle size)\n  - **`npm run eject` is forbidden** — `AGENTS.md` L274\n  - Major upgrades of `react-scripts`, `react-query`, `typescript`, or `tailwindcss` are `vsa-change-control` items (#301) — never casual\n- [ ] Note that Dependabot (#230) will open PRs and that merging them is a judgement call, not automatic.\n- [ ] State the Node version requirement (#324).\n\n## Why this is a good starter issue\n\nShort, docs-only, and it prevents a specific expensive mistake. Best written by whoever does #295, since it's a section of the same file.\n\n## Guardrails\n\n⚠️ **This documents existing policy — it does not create new policy.** `AGENTS.md` is authoritative; verify each claim against it and don't invent rules.\n\n⚠️ Do not run `npm install` or `npm audit fix` while writing this. A docs PR that rewrites the lockfile would be an unfortunate irony.\n\n🚫 Do not mass-upgrade dependencies. CRA carries substantial transitive advisory noise that version bumps won't resolve.\n\nOwning subagent: `vsa-docs-acceptance`.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hhavynn/vsa-website/issues/329/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hhavynn/vsa-website/issues/329/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1236702,"client_id":"Iv23liqTIFEtdIu6Vn1r","slug":"claude","node_id":"A_kwHOBIuudM4AEt7e","owner":{"login":"anthropics","id":76263028,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjc2MjYzMDI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76263028?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics","html_url":"https://github.com/anthropics","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Claude","description":"Run Claude Code from your GitHub Pull Requests and Issues to respond to reviewer feedback, fix CI errors, or modify code, turning it into a virtual teammate that works alongside your development pipelines.\r\n\r\nThis is built on the publicly available Claude Code SDK.","external_url":"https://anthropic.com/claude-code","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/claude","created_at":"2025-04-30T17:54:24Z","updated_at":"2026-06-01T18:22:50Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","repository_hooks":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","commit_comment","discussion","discussion_comment","issues","issue_comment","merge_queue_entry","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","push","release","repository_dispatch","status","sub_issues","workflow_dispatch","workflow_job","workflow_run"]},"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}[]